## Why This Is Asked
This problem extends the classic Longest Palindromic Subsequence (LPS) problem by allowing up to k character deletions, requiring a 3D DP formulation. It tests understanding of subsequence DP with additional constraints, careful boundary handling, and the ability to reconstruct the solution path.

## Key Concepts
- Longest Palindromic Subsequence with deletions
- 3D DP (i, j, d) where d represents remaining deletions
- Path reconstruction for deletion decisions
- Time/space complexity: O(n²·k) time, O(n²·k) space

## Code Example
```javascript
function longestPalindromicSubseqWithDeletions(s, k) {
  const n = s.length;
  const dp = Array.from({ length: n }, () =>
    Array.from({ length: n }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(0))
  );

  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    for (let d = 0; d <= k; d++) {
      dp[i][i][d] = 1;
    }
  }

  for (let len = 2; len <= n; len++) {
    for (let i = 0; i + len <= n; i++) {
      const j = i + len - 1;
      for (let d = 0; d <= k; d++) {
        if (s[i] === s[j]) {
          dp[i][j][d] = Math.max(dp[i][j][d], (len > 2 ? dp[i + 1][j - 1][d] : 0) + 2);
        }
        if (d > 0) {
          dp[i][j][d] = Math.max(dp[i][j][d], dp[i + 1][j][d - 1], dp[i][j - 1][d - 1]);
        }
      }
    }
  }

  return dp[0][n - 1][k];
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests DP with exact selection count and a non-adjacency constraint; includes reconstruction and edge handling for i-2. It also checks how to handle negative values and how to optimize space.

## Key Concepts

- 2D DP over i and t
- Non-adjacency via i-2 when taking i
- Reconstruct path from take flags
- Time/space complexity and rolling optimization

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxNonAdjacentK(A, k){
  const n = A.length;
  const NEG = -1e15;
  const dp = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  const take = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(false));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let t=0;t<=k;t++){
      dp[i][t] = Math.max(dp[i][t], dp[i-1][t]);
      if(t>0){
        if(i>=2 && dp[i-2][t-1] !== NEG){
          const val = dp[i-2][t-1] + A[i-1];
          if(val > dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t] = val; take[i][t] = true; }
        } else if(i===1 && dp[0][t-1] !== NEG){
          if(A[0] > dp[i][t]) { dp[i][t] = A[0]; take[i][t] = true; }
        }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruction omitted for brevity
}
```

