## Why This Is Asked
This question tests a harder variant of partition DP where each block's value depends on its range (max-min). It requires careful state design, precomputation of subarray values, and backtracking to output exact k non-overlapping blocks.

## Key Concepts
- 2D DP over prefix index and number of blocks
- Precomputing block values V[l][r] = max - min for all subarrays
- Reconstruction via parent pointers to output endpoints

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxRangeSubarrayValue(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const V = Array.from({ length: n }, () => Array(n).fill(0));
  for (let l = 0; l < n; l++) {
    let mx = -Infinity, mn = Infinity;
    for (let r = l; r < n; r++) {
      mx = Math.max(mx, A[r]);
      mn = Math.min(mn, A[r]);
      V[l][r] = mx - mn;
    }
  }

  const dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(-Infinity));
  const parent = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;

  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      for (let j = 1; j <= i; j++) {
        const val = dp[j - 1][t - 1] + V[j - 1][i - 1];
        if (val > dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = val;
          parent[i][t] = j;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  const blocks = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (t > 0 && parent[i][t] !== -1) {
    const j = parent[i][t];
    blocks.push([j, i]);
    i = j - 1;
    t--;
  }
  return { value: dp[n][k], blocks: blocks.reverse() };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests dynamic programming on partitioning a string into numeric substrings, including numeric parsing and reconstruction, a common interview pattern.

## Key Concepts

- DP on string partitions with exact k blocks
- Efficient substring value computation and leading-zero handling
- Path reconstruction via parent pointers
- Time/space trade-offs: O(n^2 k) time, O(nk) space

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxSumPartition(s, k) {
  const n = s.length;
  // val[i][j] = value of s[i..j-1]
  const val = Array.from({ length: n+1 }, () => Array(n+1).fill(0));
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    if (s[i] === '0') { val[i][i+1] = 0; continue; }
    let cur = 0;
    for (let j = i; j < n; j++) {
      cur = cur*10 + (s.charCodeAt(j) - 48);
      val[i][j+1] = cur;
    }
  }
  const dp = Array.from({ length: n+1 }, () => Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const par = Array.from({ length: n+1 }, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) dp[i][1] = val[0][i];
  for (let t = 2; t <= k; t++) {
    for (let i = t; i <= n; i++) {
      for (let j = t-1; j < i; j++) {
        if (s[j] === '0' && i - j > 1) continue;
        const cand = dp[j][t-1] + val[j][i];
        if (cand > dp[i][t]) { dp[i][t] = cand; par[i][t] = j; }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruct cuts
  const cuts = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (t > 0) {
    const j = par[i][t];
    cuts.push(i);
    i = j;
    t--;
  }
  cuts.push(0);
  cuts.reverse();
  return { sum: dp[n][k], cuts };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adapt to allow at most k blocks instead of exactly k?
- How would you optimize for very large n or larger k (space/time optimizations, early pruning)?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests nuanced DP on partitioning with range-dependent block costs, requiring problem decomposition, state design, and path reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- DP over prefixes and block counts
- Efficient range max computation in transitions
- Path reconstruction via parent pointers

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxScore(nums, m) {
  const n = nums.length;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array(m+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const par = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array(m+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= Math.min(i, m); t++) {
      let curMax = -Infinity;
      for (let j = i-1; j >= t-1; j--) {
        curMax = Math.max(curMax, nums[j]);
        const val = dp[j][t-1] + curMax * (i - j);
        if (val > dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = val;
          par[i][t] = j;
        }
      }
    }
  }
  // Reconstruct endpoints
  const ends = [];
  let i = n, t = m;
  while (t > 0) {
    ends.push(i);
    i = par[i][t];
    t--;
  }
  return {score: dp[n][m], ends: ends.reverse()};
}
```

